cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you refer to this evaluation, please cite it as below."
title: "Jev on a synthetic survey: does a native probability vector beat a verbalized one?"
abstract: >-
  A comparison of a decision-only model that returns a probability vector natively
  (TypeSafe Jev 1.13.0) against gpt-4.1 asked to state one, over 300 respondents and 108
  questions of the Twin-2K-500 synthetic-survey benchmark. Two decision criteria were
  written down before the runs; both failed. A follow-up arm shows that most of the
  shortfall on yes/no questions was the form of the question rather than the model.
type: dataset
authors:
  - name: "jjd-lab"
version: "1.0.0"
date-released: "2026-09-20"
license: MIT
keywords:
  - synthetic survey
  - digital twins
